From e1f2d8bb39f3eac03a2db3310bdd69632282a137 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ws07 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:34:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] Web client (S1): on a phone, a line says something
 happened while away and opens the summary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A phone shows one notice over the map, the newest, so the away summary
waited under this turn's card and only the list under その他 had it. While
a summary of this scope is not confirmed, a line under the strip now says
so (留守中の未確認の出来事 N 件) and opens that list at the summary, with
its "seen" in focus. Pressing "seen" takes the line away; closing the
notice with × does not, since × confirms nothing. Wide screens show the
summary itself and draw no line. The order and the one-notice rule of the
phone are unchanged. The screen tests that press the line come with 0010.
Needs 0003.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2bNLFpFghsNM9fsQG5
